#: ../../source/globule_README.md:15
msgid "globule.find"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:16
msgid ""
"Returns a unique array of all file or directory paths that match the "
"given globbing pattern(s). This method accepts either comma separated "
"globbing patterns or an array of globbing patterns. Paths matching "
"patterns that begin with `!` will be excluded from the returned array. "
"Patterns are processed in order, so inclusion and exclusion order is "
"significant. Patterns may be specified as function arguments or as a "
"`src` property of the options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:23
msgid ""
"The `options` object supports all [glob][] library options, along with a "
"few extras. These are the most commonly used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:25
msgid ""
"`src` This property may be used instead of specifying patterns as "
"function arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:26
msgid ""
"`filter` Either a valid [fs.Stats method "
"name](http://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/fs.html#fs_class_fs_stats) or a "
"function that will be passed the matched `src` filepath and `options` "
"object as arguments. This function should return a `Boolean` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:27
msgid ""
"`nonull` Retain globbing patterns in result set even if they fail to "
"match files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:28
msgid ""
"`matchBase` Patterns without slashes will match just the basename part. "
"Eg. this makes `*.js` work like `**/*.js`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:29
msgid ""
"`srcBase` Patterns will be matched relative to the specified path instead"
" of the current working directory. This is a synonym for `cwd`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:30
msgid ""
"`prefixBase` Any specified `srcBase` will be prefixed to all returned "
"filepaths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:34
msgid "globule.match"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:35
msgid ""
"Match one or more globbing patterns against one or more file paths. "
"Returns a uniqued array of all file paths that match any of the specified"
" globbing patterns. Both the `patterns` and `filepaths` arguments can be "
"a single string or array of strings. Paths matching patterns that begin "
"with `!` will be excluded from the returned array. Patterns are processed"
" in order, so inclusion and exclusion order is significant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:41
msgid "globule.isMatch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:42
msgid ""
"This method contains the same signature and logic as the `globule.match` "
"method, but returns `true` if any files were matched, otherwise `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:48
msgid "globule.mapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:49
msgid ""
"Given a set of source file paths, returns an array of src-dest file "
"mapping objects. Both src and dest paths may be renamed, depending on the"
" options specified. Patterns may be specified as function arguments or as"
" a `src` property of the options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:56
msgid ""
"In addition to the options the `globule.find` method supports, the "
"options object also supports these properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:58
msgid ""
"`srcBase` The directory from which patterns are matched. Any string "
"specified as `srcBase` is effectively stripped from the beginning of all "
"matched paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:59
msgid "`destBase` The specified path is prefixed to all `dest` filepaths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:60
msgid ""
"`ext` Remove anything after (and including) the first `.` in the "
"destination path, then append this value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:61
msgid ""
"`extDot` Change the behavior of `ext`, `\"first\"` and `\"last\"` will "
"remove anything after the first or last `.` in the destination filename, "
"respectively. Defaults to `\"first\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:62
msgid ""
"`flatten` Remove the path component from all matched src files. The src "
"file path is still joined to the specified destBase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:63
msgid ""
"`rename` If specified, this function will be responsible for returning "
"the final `dest` filepath. By default, it flattens paths (if specified), "
"changes extensions (if specified) and joins the matched path to the "
"`destBase`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:65
msgid "globule.findMapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/globule_README.md:66
msgid ""
"This method is a convenience wrapper around the `globule.find` and "
"`globule.mapping` methods."
msgstr ""

